# Review package: ticket 07, 77fd93e..b41d79f

## Commits
### b41d79f
perf(state): leave only the two cheap checks on the property read path

The plain-object read benchmark still ran about 4% slower with the
push/pop identity check inside getWrappedArrayMethod, which every
property read calls. Keep only Array.isArray and the typeof check
there and move the identity check, the direct pair lookup, the cache
hit and the name check into lookupArrayMethod.

### 0ab02f3
perf(state): keep the array method lookup small on the read path

Every property read calls getWrappedArrayMethod. With the direct
push/pop lookup inlined into it, the plain-object read benchmark ran
about 4% slower across three interleaved runs. Move that lookup into
getDirectArrayMethod so the body on the read path stays as small as
before.

### 21bfffd
perf(state): take a direct path for push and pop on reactive arrays

About half of the array push/pop benchmark's self time went to V8's
generic push and pop on a Proxy receiver. Run the native method on the
raw target instead and replay by hand what the get, set and delete
traps would have done: read length (and the last index for pop), set
each new index and length, delete the popped index. The replay calls
onRead, onWrite and onDelete with the arguments a direct property
access produces, runs the loop check before the equal skip inside an
effect, schedules per property inside an effect and marks the array
dirty once outside one, so no observable behavior changes. The other
five mutating methods keep the Proxy receiver; a push or pop called on
another receiver falls back to it as well.

Pin the hook call sequence and the woken subscribers for both kinds of
state against a plain Proxy over the same array as the reference.


